WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:08.321
Aircraft return to the air, ships remain available at sea, and safety-critical
engineering moves forward because authorised people can

00:08.321 --> 00:11.677
show which source and revision governs the work.

00:11.677 --> 00:19.228
The physical outcome may be a released maintenance task, an accepted
engineering change or a resolved assurance question.

00:19.228 --> 00:28.038
Before any of those decisions, someone has to trace the requirement, inspect
the evidence and identify what is missing or inconsistent.

00:28.038 --> 00:34.750
Cortessa is designed to support that investigation without taking the decision
away from the accountable person.

00:35.750 --> 00:39.313
A technical approval rarely depends on one document.

00:39.313 --> 00:45.104
Requirements connect to engineering instructions, maintenance publications,
supplier evidence, standards, safety material and

00:45.104 --> 00:45.995
configuration records.

00:45.995 --> 00:51.786
Those sources may be owned by different teams and held in disconnected
environments.

00:51.786 --> 01:00.249
The assurance problem is establishing which source is current, whether every
reference is present, whether terminology still aligns and

01:00.249 --> 01:05.149
whether the evidence applies to the platform and task under review.

01:05.149 --> 01:07.376
Search can find a page.

01:07.376 --> 01:11.830
Assurance requires the route between the pages to remain inspectable.

01:12.830 --> 01:19.919
Cortessa's target Defence deployment gives each authorised engineer a
dedicated, self-sufficient box inside the site boundary.

01:19.919 --> 01:29.667
Local documents, ingestion, index, on-device model and source viewer remain on
that box, so evidence work does not depend on a public

01:29.667 --> 01:30.553
cloud service.

01:30.553 --> 01:34.984
Audit and Ask run locally against the engineer's approved corpus.

01:34.984 --> 01:39.858
Author remains in development and requires further testing before operational
use.

01:39.858 --> 01:47.390
The engineer controls what enters the local working context and remains
responsible for every interpretation and revision.

01:48.390 --> 01:57.674
Engineer boxes are designed to connect through departmental nodes to an
on-site hub, with the complete exchange remaining inside the

01:57.674 --> 01:58.602
air-gapped site.

01:58.602 --> 02:06.494
Engineering, configuration and assurance departments retain their own scopes,
with selected cross-department sharing only where it is

02:06.494 --> 02:06.958
authorised.

02:06.958 --> 02:13.921
This is Cortessa's target site architecture, not a claim of a deployed
production network today.

02:13.921 --> 02:20.884
The governed offline revision contract and application foundations exist;
authenticated peer transport, key provisioning, delivery

02:20.884 --> 02:25.990
scheduling, backup, recovery, site assurance and physical rollout remain
deployment work.

02:26.990 --> 02:30.697
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

02:30.697 --> 02:38.112
It works across the bounded defence corpus rather than waiting for one
question at a time.

02:38.112 --> 02:44.599
It can surface missing references, supersession questions, revision
uncertainty, terminology differences and structured conflicts.

02:44.599 --> 02:51.550
Each candidate enters engineering review; it is not automatically a
certification, safety or compliance finding.

02:52.550 --> 02:57.327
Every audit result leads back to the passages that created it.

02:57.327 --> 03:03.407
The engineer can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and check
revision and applicability.

03:03.407 --> 03:08.619
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

03:08.619 --> 03:16.870
The engineer decides whether the issue is real, irrelevant, already controlled
or worth further investigation, then records the outcome

03:16.870 --> 03:18.607
through the existing process.

03:18.607 --> 03:22.950
Verified shows provenance; it does not decide which requirement governs.

03:23.950 --> 03:28.565
Technical authority cannot be outsourced to a language model.

03:28.565 --> 03:34.206
Configuration, applicability, safety significance and operational consequence
require authorised professional judgement.

03:34.206 --> 03:39.334
Cortessa makes the source route, provenance state and uncertainty visible.

03:39.334 --> 03:47.025
The responsible engineer resolves the issue and records the decision through
the organisation's approved process.

03:47.025 --> 03:55.230
Cortessa does not become the design authority, configuration authority, safety
authority, certifying body or procurement authority.

03:56.230 --> 04:04.978
When an engineer approves a revision, the revision can carry its signed
identity, content hash, parents and approved audit context

04:04.978 --> 04:09.789
through the Defence department node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

04:09.789 --> 04:16.350
Prior branches, missing parents and conflicts remain visible; arrival order
does not choose a winner.

04:16.350 --> 04:25.973
The hub cannot publish an engineer's approval, and receipt does not certify a
document or silently make it current or searchable on

04:25.973 --> 04:26.847
another box.

04:26.847 --> 04:29.909
Import and use remain explicit, engineer-governed actions.

04:29.909 --> 04:36.470
The local ledger supports inspection of system activity but never replaces the
formal engineering record.

04:37.470 --> 04:41.200
Compare matched tasks against the existing review baseline.

04:41.200 --> 04:49.593
Measure time to locate and open the governing source, reviewer effort, cited
candidate findings, accepted and rejected results,

04:49.593 --> 04:53.324
appropriate refusals and reproducibility of sampled source paths.

04:53.324 --> 05:02.649
Begin with one cleared workflow and one department, then test the controls
needed to extend it across the site architecture.

05:02.649 --> 05:09.644
For aircraft support, naval engineering and safety-critical assurance, these
remain evaluation hypotheses, not claimed operational

05:09.644 --> 05:10.110
outcomes.

05:11.110 --> 05:13.130
Bring one bounded workflow.

05:13.130 --> 05:23.735
Agree the corpus, reviewers, baseline and evidence standard, then test the
route from an engineer's local evidence work to a governed

05:23.735 --> 05:25.250
departmental revision exchange.

05:25.250 --> 05:32.825
Cortessa claims no Defence deployment, completed site rollout, platform
integration, accreditation, approval, achieved saving or

05:32.825 --> 05:33.835
readiness outcome.

05:33.835 --> 05:39.390
The architecture must be demonstrated and assured in a representative
environment.

05:39.390 --> 05:43.430
Start a conversation about a scoped Defence evaluation.
